* chan_core.lib — 3-wire hysteretic ferrite for L0 calibration
* Gate: GATE-L0-PHYSICS (docs/system_design_spec.md)
*
* Owner params (GATE-L0-PHYSICS):
*   Lm ≈ 0.00314 m
*   Ac ≈ 0.097 µm²  (documented; Phis scales numerical sense peaks)
*   Hc ≈ 150 A/m
*   Parallel damping τ ≈ 200 ns (∼1 µs-class peaking)
*
* Threshold: Ith = Hc*Lm ≈ 0.471 A·turn (N=1).
*   half-select Ic/2 = 0.3 A (one axis) → hold
*   full-select 2*(Ic/2) = 0.6 A          → flip
*
* Ngspice 42's XSPICE core(mode=2) requires H_array (hysteresis-only mode
* fails). This subcircuit is a Chan-threshold behavioral core: one shared
* flux state couples X/Y/sense windings (mutual path ≡ K≈1 Chan coupling).
* Instance count must stay ≤16 (REQ-SCALE-ANTIX).
*
* Sim assumption for drive currents lives in the calling deck (Ic=600 mA).

.subckt chan_core xp xn yp yn sp sn
.param Lm=3.14m Hc=150 Ith={Hc*Lm} Phis=1e-7 tau=200n

* Series windings: ammeter → back-EMF from shared flux (Chan mutual ≡ K≈1)
Vx xp x1 0
Ex x1 xn value={Phis*ddt(V(state))}
Vy yp y1 0
Ey y1 yn value={Phis*ddt(V(state))}
Vs sp s1 0
Es s1 sn value={Phis*ddt(V(state))}

* Ampere-turn MMF and hysteretic remanence (±1 state)
Bmmf mmf 0 V=I(Vx)+I(Vy)+I(Vs)
Cstate state 0 1n IC=1
Gstate 0 state value={(tanh(25*(V(mmf)/{Ith} + 0.85*V(state))) - V(state))/{tau}}
Rleak state 0 1G
Rdamp state 0 500k

.ends chan_core
